<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-5287] SQL: CacheConfiguration.sqlEscapeAll must affect only predefined objects</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5287</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Mentioned flag should work as follows:&lt;br/&gt;
1) If set, all object names (schema, QueryEntity (table, fields and aliases), QueryIndex (name and fields)) should be left as is.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Otherwise we should convert them to uppercase, and replace class delimiters (&quot;.&quot;, &quot;$&quot;) with underscore. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is it. This property should not be used anywhere else. Allmost all usages of &lt;tt&gt;IgniteH2Indexing.escapeName&lt;/tt&gt; should go away.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
